'''Abhinav Shukla''' is an Indian film and TV show producer. He is the producer of the film [[Ekkees Toppon Ki Salaami]]<ref name="Times of India">{{cite web|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/Why-Ekkees-Toppon-Ki-Salaami-is-a-must-watch-tells-the-cast/articleshow/44769795.cms|title= Abhinav Shukla, Producer of ETKS|work=India Times|accessdate= 27 Oct 2014}}</ref> that released recently. He is the founder and director of the production company [[Nautanki Films]].<ref name="Nautanki Films">{{cite web|url=http://nautankifilms.com/promoter.html |title=Abhinav Shukla, Nautank Films |publisher=Nautanki Films |accessdate=27 Oct 2014 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20141028160536/http://nautankifilms.com/promoter.html |archivedate=2014-10-28 }}</ref>

==Professional life==
After starting his company he produced shows such as [[Baba Aiso Varr Dhoondo]] (aired on [[Imagine TV]]), [[Do Dil Ek Jaan]] (aired on [[Life Ok]]) and [[Madhubala - Ek Ishq Ek Junoon]] (aired on [[Colors TV]]) Nautanki News, Lete hai Khabar and Nadaniya. His production house also contributed in some episodes crime patrol. He then got into film production with the comic satire Ekkees Toppon Ki Salaami.<ref name="TellyChakkar">{{cite web|url=http://www.tellychakkar.com/movie/interview/ekkees-toppon-ki-salaami-would-appeal-every-aam-aadmi-abhinav-shukla-141008|title= Abhinav Shukla speaks about ETKS|work=Telly Chakkar|accessdate= 27 Oct 2014}}</ref> The first look of the film was launched by [[Shah Rukh Khan]]<ref name="Deccan Chronicle reports">{{cite web|url=http://www.deccanchronicle.com/140812/entertainment-bollywood/gallery/shah-rukh-khan-unveils-ekeess-topon-ki-salami-trailer|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140813073427/http://www.deccanchronicle.com/140812/entertainment-bollywood/gallery/shah-rukh-khan-unveils-ekeess-topon-ki-salami-trailer|url-status=dead|archive-date=13 August 2014|title= Shah Rukh Khan launched first look of ETKS|work=Deccan Chronicle|accessdate= 27 Oct 2014}}</ref>

Abhinav also headed the strategy and management team at B.A.G Films & Media Ltd.<ref name="Economic Times">{{cite web|url=http://articles.economictimes.indiatimes.com/2010-07-01/news/28418483_1_bag-films-media-channel-talks-with-private-equity|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141211083450/http://articles.economictimes.indiatimes.com/2010-07-01/news/28418483_1_bag-films-media-channel-talks-with-private-equity|url-status=dead|archive-date=11 December 2014|title= Abhinav Shukla on BAG Films raising capital|work=Economic Times|accessdate= 27 Oct 2014}}</ref> He played a vital role in setting up the channels [[News 24 (India)|News 24]] and [[E24 (TV channel)|E24]].

He also serves as the director and promoter <ref name="AFAQS">{{cite web| url=https://www.afaqs.com/news/company_briefs/?id=46610_GEMS+Education+increases+its+network+of+schools|title= Abhinav Shukla, Promoter of Greater Valley School |publisher=AFAQS|accessdate= 27 Oct 2014}}</ref> of well known Great Valley School,<ref name="Greater Valley School">{{cite web| url=http://www.greatervalleyschool.com/about-us/messagenote-from-the-board/directors-message| archive-url=https://archive.today/20141028143007/http://www.greatervalleyschool.com/about-us/messagenote-from-the-board/directors-message| url-status=dead| archive-date=28 October 2014| title=Abhinav Shukla, Greater Valley School| publisher=Greater Valley School| accessdate=27 Oct 2014}}</ref> Greater Noida.

==Education==
Abhinav holds an MBA from Maastricht School of Management, Netherlands in International Finance (Marketing & Strategy).<ref name="Bloomberg Businessweek">{{cite web| url=http://investing.businessweek.com/research/stocks/people/person.asp?personId=62100405&ticker=BAGF:IN&previousCapId=22860007&previousTitle=B.A.G.%20FILMS%20%26%20MEDIA%20LTD|title= Abhinav Shukla, Profiled by Bloomberg BusinessWeek|work=Business Week|accessdate= 27 Oct 2014}}{{dead link|date=April 2023|bot=medic}}{{cbignore|bot=medic}}</ref>

